    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1125">

                <pb facs="0811" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            British Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Ambassador of Great
                    Britain, and has the honor to enclose herewith, for his information, a copy of a
                    telegram dated May 1 from the special representative of the Department of State
                    at El Paso, quoting a <pb facs="0812" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/> telegram dated
                    April 30th, from General Carranza, in relation to the resumption of work in the
                    Tampico oil district and the suggested neutralization of certain zones for the
                    purpose of carrying on operations in this district.</p>
                <p>A copy of this telegram has also been transmitted to the Secretary of the Navy,
                    with the request that the substance thereof be immediately telegraphed to
                    Admiral Fletcher, for his information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-02"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
